              "text": "どろぼう (dorobō) is a mixed word, native and Sino-Japanese: doro, \"mud\", is native Japanese, and bō, \"stick\", is a Chinese character read with its on'yomi, a reading borrowed from Chinese (Middle Chinese baewngX) (JMdict, KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription). How the two came together is not settled."
